  "title": "Advanced Word Order",
  "titleRussian": "Порядок слов (углублённый)",
  "description": "Information structure and emphasis",
  "descriptionRussian": "Актуальное членение и эмфаза",
  "imageName": "text.line.first.and.arrowtriangle.forward",
  "intro": "Russian word order is flexible but meaningful. THEME-RHEME: Known info (theme) comes first, new info (rheme) comes last for emphasis. NEUTRAL: Иван читает книгу (Ivan is reading a book). EMPHASIS ON DOER: Книгу читает Иван (It's IVAN who's reading). EMPHASIS ON OBJECT: Иван книгу читает (Ivan is reading a BOOK). INVERSION: Placing verbs first creates drama or questions. CLITIC PLACEMENT: Short pronouns/particles (же, ли, бы) follow the first stressed word. Master word order for natural, nuanced communication.",
  "rules": [
    "Theme (known) first, rheme (new) last: Книгу читает Иван (emphasis on Ivan)",
    "Neutral SVO: Иван читает книгу (no special emphasis)",
    "Verb-initial for drama/questions: Пришёл Иван! (Ivan arrived!)",
    "Clitics after first stressed word: Он же знает! (He DOES know!)"
  ],
  "examples": [
    "Иван читает книгу. (Ivan is reading a book., neutral)",
    "Книгу читает Иван. (It's Ivan who's reading the book., emphasis on Ivan)",
    "Иван книгу читает. (Ivan is reading a book., emphasis on reading/book)",
    "Пришла весна! (Spring has come!, dramatic verb-first)"
  ],
