    "grammarFocus": "Emphasis: Звонил Иван (new info 'Ivan' at end)",
    "hints": [
      "In Russian, new/emphasized information goes at the END of the sentence. If 'Ivan' is the new info, what comes first?"
    ],
    "explanations": [
      "Russian word order places new information (rheme) at the end: 'Звонил Иван' emphasizes WHO called (Ivan is the new info). Starting with the verb puts focus on the subject at the end. 'Иван звонил' would emphasize what Ivan did, not who called."
